{
  "category": "Cotton Puff Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "When attacked, it escapes by shooting cotton from its body. The cotton serves as a decoy to distract the attacker.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "They go wherever the wind takes them. On rainy days, their bodies are heavier, so they take shelter beneath big trees.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "Perhaps because they feel more at ease in a group, they stick to others they find. They end up looking like a cloud.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Perhaps because they feel more at ease in a group, they stick to others they find. They end up looking like a cloud.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "When attacked, it escapes by shooting cotton from its body. The cotton serves as a decoy to distract the attacker.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Perhaps because they feel more at ease in a group, they stick to others they find. They end up looking like a cloud.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "When attacked, it escapes by shooting cotton from its body. The cotton serves as a decoy to distract the attacker.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Perhaps because they feel more at ease in a group, they stick to others they find. They end up looking like a cloud.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it finds others of its kind, they all stick together. When enough of them have collected, the mass resembles a cumulonimbus cloud.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pillows and beds stuffed with cotton exhaled by Cottonee are soft and puffy, light and airy— altogether top quality.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "To protect itself, it shoots cotton from its body. When it gets wet in the rain, its cotton grows moist and heavy, and it can’t move as well.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "When attacked, it expels cotton from its body to create a diversion. The cotton it loses grows back in quickly.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It shoots cotton from its body to protect itself. If it gets caught up in hurricane-strength winds, it can get sent to the other side of the Earth.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Weaving together the cotton of both Cottonee and Eldegoss produces exquisite cloth that’s highly prized by many luxury brands.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
